=71dc2a904bc67926"},{"ObjectID":29446,"Title":"Non vouloir (Not to Want)","Artist":"Pablo Picasso","Date":"1942","Medium":"Book with one engraving and drypoints (frontispiece); four prints from line blocks with added engraving, printed in black, accompanying the letterpress text; supplementary suite of three engraving and drypoints (color variants of the frontispiece) and nineteen line-block prints (sixteen made by printing the same four blocks in four color variants: turquoise, yellow, red, and green; three made by printing the same four blocks in various superimposed color combinations); rebound with Hugnet’s handwritten manuscript of the text in red ink (fifty-seven leaves); publisher’s original tan paper cover. Bespoke rebinding and slipcase by F. Saulnier. Rebinding: covers of full red leather over boards; blind tooling around raised bands and gold-tooled title on spine; red and white silk doublures and red endpapers; red-and-black silk endbands; multicolor silk bookmark.","CreditLine":"The Louis E. Stern Collection","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/29446","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjE3Mzg2NyJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=828ce31a9e808a81","OnView":1},{"ObjectID":30440,"Title":"Plate (page 104) from Cirque de l'étoile filante (The Shooting Star Circus)","Artist":"Georges Rouault","Date":"1938","Medium":"Wood engraving from an illustrated book with seventy-four wood engravings and seventeen aquatint and etchings (eleven with drypoint)","CreditLine":"The Louis E. Stern Collection","URL":"https://www.moma.org/collection/works/30440","ImageURL":"https://www.moma.org/media/W1siZiIsIjE4OTUwNyJdLFsicCIsImNvbnZlcnQiLCItcmVzaXplIDEwMjR4MTAyNFx1MDAzZSJdXQ.jpg?sha=ef2af19abc9f4aad"},{"ObjectID":32428,"Title":"Visions of Marquis de Sade (plate 6) from Charenton","Artist":"José Luis Cuevas","Date":"1965, published 1966","Medium":"Lithograph from an illustrated book with fifteen lithographs (including tit